       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg for adults. An overdose at that level can cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. That risk applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? These are the usual adult dosing options:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg orally once daily.\n- **Titration:** increase to the maximum of 10 mg once daily if needed.\n- **Lower starting dose of 2.5 mg daily:** for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf you tell me the dose you want, for example 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, I'll enter it right away. If you intended something else, such as a different drug, please tell me. If you need more than the labeled maximum, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy. Adding a second agent from a different class is usually safer than raising the amlodipine dose."
      }
