      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. The risk of severe hypotension and shock is too high for me to enter it on an unverified statement.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily now. That's the maximum, and you can add a second antihypertensive agent if you need more effect.\n- **Involve pharmacy or a second prescriber.** If you think a dose above the label is justified, they can review it and document the rationale. Orders like that normally go through a pharmacist-verified process or an institutional override, not through me.\n- **Tell me about the clinical goal.** If you describe the condition and the blood pressure or angina target, I can help you work out alternatives, such as combination therapy.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter 10 mg once daily or a different dose."
      }
     ],
